  "clarifyingQuestions": [
    "Should extra arguments be rejected or ignored?",
    "Should nested object schemas be supported?",
    "Should validation return the first error or all errors?"
  ],
  "followUps": [
    "Add enum constraints for fields.",
    "Add nested object validation.",
    "Add authorization checks after shape validation."
  ],
  "followUpGuide": [
    "Enums are field-level value checks after type validation.",
    "",
    "Nested schemas need recursive validation with path-aware error messages.",
    "",
    "Authorization belongs after schema validation; a well-shaped call can still be unsafe."
  ],
  "complexityAnalysis": [
    "- Let f be the number of fields across args and schema maps, and e the number of extra arguments. With bounded-length names and average constant-time hash lookups, time is O(f + e log e): extra fields must be sorted. Auxiliary space is O(f), including allowed-field sets, merged schema fields, sorted extras, and returned errors. Unbounded field names also add string hashing, comparison, and error-construction costs.",
    "- Nested validation is a follow-up. Its cost depends on visited values, constraints, path construction, and collected errors; recursive stack space alone is O(depth). The current validator checks only top-level fields."
  ],
  "solutionGuide": [
    "Validate name first, then required fields, then extra fields, then types in schema order.",
    "",
    "```python",
    "def validate_call(call: dict, schemas: dict) -> list[str]:",
    "    name = call.get(\"name\")",
    "    if name not in schemas:",
    "        return [f\"unknown_tool:{name}\"]",
    "",
    "    args = call.get(\"args\", {})",
    "    schema = schemas[name]",
    "    required = schema.get(\"required\", {})",
    "    optional = schema.get(\"optional\", {})",
    "    allowed = set(required) | set(optional)",
    "    errors = []",
    "",
    "    for field in required:",
    "        if field not in args:",
    "            errors.append(f\"missing:{field}\")",
    "    for field in sorted(set(args) - allowed):",
    "        errors.append(f\"extra:{field}\")",
    "",
    "    type_map = {\"str\": str, \"bool\": bool, \"list\": list, \"dict\": dict}",
    "    for field, expected in {**required, **optional}.items():",
    "        if field not in args:",
    "            continue",
    "        value = args[field]",
    "        if expected == \"int\":",
    "            ok = isinstance(value, int) and not isinstance(value, bool)",
    "        elif expected == \"float\":",
    "            ok = isinstance(value, float) or (",
    "                isinstance(value, int) and not isinstance(value, bool)",
    "            )",
    "        else:",
    "            ok = isinstance(value, type_map[expected])",
    "        if not ok:",
    "            errors.append(f\"type:{field}:{expected}\")",
    "    return errors",
    "```"
  ]
